                    <ul style="list-style:none; padding:0; font-size:12px; color:#cbd5e1; line-height:1.7;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">🏢 <strong>Petabyte Server Centers:</strong> Meta & Google store raw bloated JSON and uncompressed schemas across warehouse-scale server farms consuming billions in electricity and cooling.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">🔓 <strong>Single Point of Disaster:</strong> If one database or S3 bucket is leaked, all user records are exposed in plain-text. Hackers steal entire files at once.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">🐢 <strong>Linear Search Latency:</strong> Scanning massive unindexed tables degrades performance during peak query loads.</li>
                        <li>💰 <strong>Infinite Cloud Inefficiency:</strong> Companies pay millions every month just to store redundant whitespace, duplicate keys, and static metadata.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

